|~ What is declared under `::keyword`: the refusal of its
   constructor, and the comparisons of keywords, which compare two
   keywords by their names in the one order. ~|

:keyword/construct
  |~~ Reads a keyword as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError
  |~~ `::keyword` reads its payload as the keyword it is; a string
      becomes one by `keyword`.
  ~~|

:keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError/refusesAString
  |~~ A string payload is refused; `keyword` turns a string into one. ~~|
  ::law~(::keyword"k" !| [type /actualType] | eq [::keyword/PayloadNotKeywordError ::string])

:keyword/gt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows the name of the keyword the
      call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gt/ordersByName
  |~~ `:b` follows `:a`. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gt :a | eq true)

:keyword/gt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gt/than/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gt/greater
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/gte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name follows or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/gte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A keyword follows or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gte :b | eq true)

:keyword/gte/ordersByName
  |~~ `:b` follows `:a`. ~~|
  ::law~(:b | gte :a | eq true)

:keyword/gte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/gte/than/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/gte/atLeast
  |~~ Whether the subject comes after the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lt
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes the name of the keyword the
      call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lt/ordersByName
  |~~ `:a` precedes `:b`. ~~|
  ::law~(:a | lt :b | eq true)

:keyword/lt/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lt/than/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lt/less
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/lte
  |~~ Whether the subject's name precedes or equals the name of the
      keyword the call gives.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/lte/holdsOfItself
  |~~ A keyword precedes or equals itself. ~~|
  ::law~(:a | lte :a | eq true)

:keyword/lte/than
  |~~ The value the subject is compared with. ~~|
  ~(/0)

:keyword/lte/than/NotKeywordError
  |~~ The than is a keyword. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword)

:keyword/lte/atMost
  |~~ Whether the subject comes before the value compared or equals it. ~~|
  ::boolean

:keyword/keyword
  |~~ The name of the keyword, as a string: the reverse of `keyword` on
      a string, so `"foo" | keyword | keyword` answers `"foo"`.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/keyword/answersTheName
  |~~ A keyword answers its name as a string. ~~|
  ::law~(:foo | keyword | eq "foo")

:keyword/keyword/keepsASpace
  |~~ A name with a space keeps it. ~~|
  ::law~(:"foo bar" | keyword | eq "foo bar")

:keyword/keyword/text
  |~~ The name of the keyword, a string. ~~|
  ::string

:keyword/runLaws
  |~~ The results of the laws under the binding the keyword names in
      its scope, one `{:law :says :actual :ok :error}` per law, `:law`
      its address and `:says` its page, the claim it proves. A keyword
      after it runs the laws of the member the binding holds under it.
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:keyword/runLaws/runsTheLawsUnderTheName
  |~~ The laws under the name the keyword reads run. ~~|
  ::law~(:limit |~~ A limit. ~~| 10 | :limit/holds |~~ It holds. ~~| ::law~(true) | :limit | runLaws * /ok | eq [true])

:keyword/runLaws/anchor
  |~~ The anchor within the page, null when it gives none. ~~|
  ~(at 0)

:keyword/runLaws/anchor/NotKeywordOrNullError
  |~~ The anchor is a keyword or null. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::keyword ::null)

:keyword/runLaws/results
  |~~ One result for each law: the law, its claim, what it answered and whether it held. ~~|
  ::vec

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError
  |~~ `runLaws` found no declaration of the name it read, as `binding`
      finds none.
      ::link~(::any/binding/UnknownNameError | doc)
  ~~|

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError/refusesANameNothingDeclares
  |~~ A name nothing declares is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(:nonexistent-binding | runLaws !| [type /name] | eq [::keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError :nonexistent-binding])

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError/namesWhereTheWordLives
  |~~ A word's name is refused with the addresses where the word lives. ~~|
  ::law~(:filter | runLaws !| /addresses | has ::vec/filter)

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError/name
  |~~ The name the axis read, a keyword or a tag. ~~|
  #[::keyword ::tag]

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError/addresses
  |~~ The addresses of the pages of that name, one for each kind that answers it. ~~|
  ::set

:keyword/runLaws/UnknownNameError/nearest
  |~~ The names nearest to it in spelling. ~~|
  ::vec
